Good morning.

I am happy to announce the release of KLog 0.9.0.

(You are receiving this email because you has been involved with KLog in
one time... if you don't want to receive more emails about KLog just ask
me to remove from my KLog contact list!)

The official announce is here:
 =20
http://jaime.robles.es/klog-0-9-0-released-kontest-goes-back-to-klog-agai=
n/  =20


You can download from the KLog's download page:
   http://jaime.robles.es/klog/klog-download/

You can subscribe to the mailinglist:
   http://jaime.robles.es/klog/klogs-mailing-lists/


The main things to know about this release is that I have come back from
Kontest to KLog so this KLog is able to run in Linux, OSX & Windows,
answering a request that I have received MANY times, to make KLog able
to run in several platforms... so now we have it!

As far as I know, KLog is the only hamradio logging software able tor
run in several operating systems and it is Free Software!

I would like to ask the translators of previous releases of KLog for an
extra effort to translate KLog again as today it is only in English and
Spanish (please write me if you want to help KLog!).

As KLog has been fully rewritten since KLog 0.6.2, I am expecting some
feature missing and probably some new bugs.
Please report any bug, suggestion or feature request and I will add it
to the roadmap (the TODO list in the sources package).

The changelog of this KLog 0.9.0 releases says the following:

November-2014 -- 0.9.0
-- Ensures the ASCII requirement of ADIF.
-- Updated the Preferences dialog.
-- Added the About Qt help menu.
-- Bugfix: Selected DX-Cluster servers were not used to connect.
-- Bugfix: When selecting QSL received/sent with right click, date was
not updated.
-- Bugfix: Fixed the FileManager::adifReadLog to be able to read logs
with several lines per QSO.
-- Some other minor bugfixes.
-- New feature: It is possible to show Imperial System (Miles instead of
Km) data. (TNX -- KF5JNU)
-- New feature: It is possible to mark/look for & export requested QSL.
-- New feature: It is possible to automatically mark(or not) a QSL as
requested by the DX when the DX's card is received.
-- New feature: It is possible to show (or not) the callsign used in the
search box.
-- New feature: KLog uses bigcty.csv for normal DX & will use cty.csv
for contesting.


Enjoy KLog!
Jaime, EA4TV

